  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>RWA distributed value fell 6.6% over 30D:</strong> On-chain RWA distributed value at $14.82B (6.6% lower over 30D) hints that tokenized asset growth paused or reversed\u2014more consistent with risk-off allocation or redemptions than a pure news cycle. Related: <a href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/modern-treasury-seeks-us-trust-bank-charter-for-stablecoin-custody?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Modern Treasury seeks US trust bank charter for digital asset custody</a> (CoinTelegraph).</li><li><strong>Tokenized U.S. Treasuries remain the institutional bridge into RWAs:</strong> adoption is strongest where products plug into cash management, collateral, and liquidity workflows. Related: <a href=\"https://thedefiant.io/converge/tradfi-and-fintech/dune-flags-yield-shortfall-at-tokenized-money-funds\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Dune Flags Yield Shortfall at Tokenized Money Funds</a> (The Defiant).</li><li><strong>Institutional commitments are still a leading share signal:</strong> Bank and asset-manager distribution deals often shift platform and network leadership before headline RWA totals fully catch up. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/10/05/kraken-operator-payward-and-singapore-gulf-bank-platform-for-24-7-institutional-crypto-settlement\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Kraken operator Payward and Singapore Gulf Bank partner for 24/7 institutional crypto settlement</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Regulatory framing still decides product access:</strong> Clearer rules tend to unlock balance-sheet participation and collateral workflows even when aggregate on-chain totals reprice slowly. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/10/05/u-s-cftc-joins-sec-in-proposing-crypto-regulations-though-spot-market-gap-lingers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">U.S. CFTC joins SEC in proposing crypto regulations, though spot-market gap lingers</a> (CoinDesk).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
